  "id": "rationality",
  "term": "rationality",
  "definition": "Rationality is the quality of updating beliefs and judgments in a way that appropriately weighs prior expectations and new evidence. In this source, it is treated not simply as strict Bayesian correctness, but as adaptive inference shaped by limited cognitive resources, learned reliability, and uncertainty in the environment.",
